  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Giving good feedback is a skill you learn through practice. The goal here is to understand the basic rules of giving good feedback and practice them until you've gotten better at each of them.\n\n### One step at a time\n\nBegin by reviewing the [Rules for Giving Feedback](Glint_Manager_Rules_for_Giving_Feedback). Then choose one area where you'd like to improve and practice it. Then, once you feel you've made progress, move on to the next.\n\nTry to practice as many as you can to get better at giving your team feedback.\n\n[Characteristics of effective feedback](video \"LiL3_Effective_Feedback\")\n\n**Watch**: *Characteristics of effective feedback*\n\n---",
